# Milestone: M3
# Covers: variables declared in '&' and ',' branches are unscoped into the
#         parent environment (not local to the branch block).
# blocked: `var a & var b` parallel-declare not supported — parse error (deferred-v1.x)
#   (T39 chk-driver reason stale; the chk driver handles fork separators fine)
# matrix-row: separator-and
#
# Reason (updated v0.13.5 probe):
#   `var a & var b` — the parser rejects `&` immediately after the var name
#   with "unexpected token" (the `&` is not `=` and is not a separator the
#   var-decl arm expects).  `var a , var b` parses as two separate statements
#   separated by `,` (fork-detach noop) — no error, but both vars install
#   into the same scope as ordinary chunk-top bindings; no unscoping occurs.
#   The §7.1 shared-frame unscoping semantic (variables declared in fork
#   branches visible in the parent scope) is not yet implemented
#   (deferred-v1.x per language-compatibility-matrix).
#   Activatable when parallel-var-declare and unscoping semantics land.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M5 with unscoping semantics):
# # { var a & var b; a; b; void };
# # { var a, a; void };
